---
layout: base.njk
title: Browse
description: "Browse AtlasLatino by field, type, or country — talks or people."
permalink: "/browse/"
---
<h1 class="visually-hidden">Browse</h1>

{#
  One list per axis (field / type / country). Each row carries two counts:
  Talks (links to that filter's research feed) and People (links to the
  researchers connected to it). Single-axis only — no combining filters
  (see src/_data/browsePages.js / browsePeople.js).

  Fields and types come from their fixed lists so the order matches the
  rest of the site; countries are alphabetical, not by count — same
  reasoning as the stats page: nothing here should read as a ranking.

  Talks counts come from browsePages (page 0 of each filter's feed);
  People counts come from browsePeople. A row only appears if it has at
  least one talk; the People cell shows "—" if that axis value has talks
  but somehow no resolved people (shouldn't happen, but never links to an
  empty page).
#}

{% macro browseRow(label, talksUrl, talksCount, peopleUrl, peopleCount) %}
  <li class="browse-row">
    <span class="browse-label">{{ label }}</span>
    <a class="browse-cell" href="{{ talksUrl | url }}">{{ talksCount }}</a>
    {% if peopleCount %}
      <a class="browse-cell" href="{{ peopleUrl | url }}">{{ peopleCount }}</a>
    {% else %}
      <span class="browse-cell browse-cell--empty">—</span>
    {% endif %}
  </li>
{% endmacro %}

<div class="section-bar section-bar--browse">
  <h2 class="section-title">Browse by field</h2>
  <div class="browse-heads"><span>Talks</span><span>People</span></div>
</div>
<ul class="browse-list browse-list--two">
  {% for fp in browsePages.fieldPages %}
    {% if fp.pageNumber == 0 %}
      {{ browseRow(fp.label, fp.url, fp.totalEntries, "/field/" + fp.basePath.split("/")[2] + "/people/", browsePeople.fieldCounts[fp.basePath.split("/")[2]]) }}
    {% endif %}
  {% endfor %}
</ul>

